# SIM Pre-Design Questionnaire (for Google Forms)

**Purpose:** Gather input from students, staff, and landlords/villa mates on campus
security incidents and reporting preferences, to inform the design of the SIM
(Security Incident Mapping) platform.

Copy each section below into Google Forms. Use the "Section" feature so each
respondent only sees the section relevant to their role.

---

## Section 0 — Respondent Type
*(Add this as the first question, using "Go to section based on answer")*

1. **Which best describes you?** *(Multiple choice, required)*
   - Student (living on campus)
   - Student (living off campus)
   - Staff (academic or non-academic)
   - Landlord / Property Manager (off-campus lodging)

---

## Section 1 — Students (on & off campus)

2. Where do you currently reside? *(Short answer)*
3. Have you ever witnessed or experienced a security incident on or around campus?
   *(Multiple choice: Yes / No / Prefer not to say)*
4. If yes, what type of incident was it? *(Checkboxes, allow "Other")*
   - Theft / Stealing
   - Stabbing / Assault
   - Rape / Sexual Assault
   - Burglary
   - Suspicious activity
   - Other: ______
5. Did you report the incident to anyone (security, hostel warden, police)?
   *(Multiple choice: Yes / No)*
6. If you did not report it, why not? *(Checkboxes)*
   - Didn't know who to contact
   - Too slow / inconvenient
   - Feared retaliation or exposure
   - Didn't think it would be acted on
   - Other: ______
7. Would you use a mobile/web app to report incidents anonymously?
   *(Linear scale 1 = Definitely not, 5 = Definitely yes)*
8. What information would you want to see on an incident map? *(Checkboxes)*
   - Location of recent incidents
   - Incident type/severity
   - Whether it's been resolved
   - Safety tips for the area
9. Any additional comments or suggestions? *(Paragraph, optional)*

---

## Section 2 — Staff

2. What is your role? *(Short answer, e.g. lecturer, admin staff, security)*
3. Have you observed or been informed of recurring security issues around campus?
   *(Multiple choice: Yes / No)*
4. Which locations do you consider highest risk? *(Short answer)*
5. Would a centralized incident reporting/mapping tool help your unit respond faster?
   *(Linear scale 1 = Not at all, 5 = Very much)*
6. What features would be most useful to you as staff? *(Checkboxes)*
   - Real-time incident alerts
   - Ability to verify/update incident status
   - Statistics/reports for administration
   - Direct link to security response team
7. Any additional comments? *(Paragraph, optional)*

---

## Section 3 — Landlords / Property Managers (off-campus lodging)

2. How many students currently live in your property/properties? *(Short answer)*
3. Have there been any security incidents at your property in the last year?
   *(Multiple choice: Yes / No / Not sure)*
4. If yes, what type? *(Checkboxes, allow "Other")*
5. What security measures do you currently have in place? *(Checkboxes)*
   - Fencing/gate
   - Security guard
   - Lighting
   - CCTV
   - None currently
6. Would you be willing to receive alerts about incidents reported near your property?
   *(Multiple choice: Yes / No)*
7. Would you support your tenants using an app to report incidents that occur at
   your property? *(Multiple choice: Yes / No / Not sure)*
8. Any additional comments? *(Paragraph, optional)*

---

### Setup notes for Google Forms
- Enable "Collect email addresses" only if you need follow-up; otherwise keep
  anonymous to encourage honest responses about crime.
- Use **Sections** (the "Add section" icon) to branch by respondent type from
  Question 1, via **"Go to section based on answer."**
- Set the form to **accept responses without sign-in** so landlords/staff without
  a campus email can respond.
